<h1>Pope Addresses Global Cybersecurity Summit at Vatican</h1>
<p class=3D"byline">By Staff Reporter &lt;newsroom@cnn.com&gt; | Updated April 19, 2024</p>
<p>Security researchers disclosed a critical vulnerability tracked as CVE-2024-1234
affecting millions of devices worldwide. The flaw, discovered by analysts at
<a href=3D"https://www.cnn.com/tech/security">CNN Tech</a>, allows remote attackers
to execute arbitrary code on unpatched systems.</p>
<p>Investigators identified command-and-control infrastructure at IP address
8.8.8.8, a server known to researchers at <a href=3D"https://www.cnn.com/">CNN</a>.
The domain <strong>www.cnn.com</strong> was referenced throughout the report as
the primary source.</p>
<p>The Vatican network team confirmed patching began on April 18, 2024. Full
remediation is expected by end of month.</p>
